## EXP14

Aim:
To develop a Java program to perform file operations using
I/O streams, readers, writers, and buffered streams.


Procedure:
Create a Java program.
Create a file using FileWriter.
Write data using BufferedWriter.
Read the file using BufferedReader and display the output.


Result:
Thus, the Java program was executed successfully and file reading 
and writing operations were performed using buffered streams.

## PROGRAM 14

import java.io.*;

class FileDemo {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        BufferedWriter bw = new BufferedWriter(new FileWriter("data.txt"));
        bw.write("Welcome to Java File Handling");
        bw.close();

        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new FileReader("data.txt"));
        String s;
        while ((s = br.readLine()) != null) {
            System.out.println(s);
        }
        br.close();
    }
}


## EXP 15


Aim:
To develop a Java program to store and retrieve objects using serialization 
and deserialization.


Procedure:
Create a class implementing Serializable.
Create an object and assign values.
Save the object using ObjectOutputStream.
Retrieve the object using ObjectInputStream and display it.


Result:
Thus, the Java program was executed successfully to perform serialization 
and deserialization of objects.



## PROGRAM 15


import java.io.*;

class Student implements Serializable {
    int id = 101;
    String name = "Gokul";

    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        Student s = new Student();

        ObjectOutputStream out = new ObjectOutputStream(
            new FileOutputStream("data.txt"));
        out.writeObject(s);
        out.close();

        ObjectInputStream in = new ObjectInputStream(
            new FileInputStream("data.txt"));
        Student obj = (Student) in.readObject();

        System.out.println(obj.id);
        System.out.println(obj.name);
        in.close();
    }
}

